// CMUdict-Derived English Homophone Rules
// =========================================
//
// Experimental broad-coverage extension for exact-pronunciation homophone
// matching against CMUdict-style American English pronunciations. These rules
// map alphabetic CMUdict homophone spellings to uppercase ARPAbet-derived
// canonical strings. Uppercase replacements are intentionally used so the
// lowercase orthographic rules in the primary English dialect do not rewrite
// the pronunciation code after this extension fires.
//
// Scope: all alphabetic CMUdict pronunciation groups with at least two base
// words after the benchmark loader normalization used by examples/scientific_eval.rs.
// Alternate pronunciations are retained as separate rules for the same word.
// Patterns and replacements are quoted to avoid LLev keyword-token ambiguity
// in generated lexical entries such as "calif".
// Keep separate from american.llev because this is an evaluation/research
// extension rather than a general dialect model.

@name "CMUdict-Derived English Homophones"
@version "0.2.0"
@author "liblevenshtein scientific evaluation"
@description "CMUdict-derived ARPAbet canonical homophone rules for benchmark and research evaluation"

